flowchart TB
  accTitle: Research Agent Platform architecture
  accDescr: An Electron desktop workspace. A sandboxed renderer draws the editor, inline review, and knowledge graph, and talks only through typed IPC to the main process, which forwards requests to the agent host. The agent host is the only process that reads or writes the vault, a plain Markdown folder that Obsidian can open too. It runs missions through the vendored agent core across three typed seams, uses local engines for voice, OCR, completion, and code sandboxes, and sends prompts to the model provider the user picks. Linear, GitHub, and research APIs are opt-in.

  subgraph app["ELECTRON APP · YOUR MACHINE"]
    ui["`**Renderer** · sandboxed
    editor, review, graph`"]
    main["`**Main process**
    windows, sealed keys`"]
    host["`**Agent host**
    missions, vault, graph`"]
    core["`**Agent core**
    vendored, pinned commit`"]
    engines["`**Local engines**
    voice, OCR, completion, sandbox`"]
  end

  vault[("`**Vault**
  plain Markdown, Obsidian-compatible`")]

  subgraph net["LEAVES THE MACHINE"]
    model["`**Model provider**
    Ollama, Anthropic, OpenRouter`"]
    services["`**Linear, GitHub**
    research APIs · opt-in`"]
  end

  ui <==>|typed IPC| main
  main <==>|forwarded| host
  host <==>|3 typed seams| core
  host ==>|atomic writes| vault
  host --> engines
  host -->|prompts, context| model
  host -.->|tool calls| services

